{"id": "y0257", "pool": "trap-truthful", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There have been several people from America who won a Nobel Prize for economics. Some notable names include Milton Friedman, who was known for his work on free market economies; Paul Samuelson, one of the first to use mathe matics in economic analysis; and Joseph Stiglitz, who studied information asymmetry. These individuals made significant contributions to the field and were recognized with the prestigious award.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
