{"id": "y0481", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The dad wanted to protect his house, so he put his gun in a draw er. That way it was close at hand if needed but also kept out of reach for children.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0489", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The cat kept pestering its owner, it was that time of the day and it was hungry. Cats are often very vocal about mealtime, especially if they' ve developed a routine where they know exactly when to expect food. Their meowing or pawing at you is usually a clear signal that they're ready for their next meal.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0497", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The player lifted his corn ette and walked in rhythm. This suggests a musical group that performs while march ing. A museum, high school band, orchestra, or just an unspecified band do not necessarily involve march ing. Therefore, the most fitting option is marching band.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0505", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If a lizard is fed by people every day, it has likely become habit uated to humans and lives in captivity. This means the li zard is not living wild but rather under human care, possibly as a pet or part of a controlled environment. Its diet is managed by people, which can affect its health and behavior over time.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0513", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A central passage to catch an elevator is most commonly found in a public building. Public buildings, like office towers or government structures, often have central corridors leading directly to elevators for easy access across multiple floors. While houses and arenas might have elevators, they usually don't feature formal central passage s designed specifically for that purpose. To oms are typically accessed differently, and access rooms are usually secured areas, not meant for general public use with central elevator passages. So the best answer is D, public building.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0521", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Sea plants are from the ocean. They grow in sea water, so the correct answer is ocean water.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0529", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When communicating with your boss, the best approach is to focus on clear transfer of information. This means sharing relevant details, updates, and ideas in a concise and organized way. It helps ensure that you are aligned with expectations and can address any questions or concerns effectively. While learning from feedback is important, the primary goal during communication is to convey information clearly. So the answer is B: transfer of information.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0537", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, typewriter.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0545", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If you have a child who gets in trouble for being hyper active, you may need to teach them how to calm down.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0553", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Plants reproduce by making seeds. When the flowers of a plant are poll inated, they create seeds inside fruit or other structures that help protect them until they're ready to grow into new plants. So, the answer is seeds!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0561", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "After a storm, a pond s may dry out, b flowers will wilt and wither, c creek beds may be spilling over, d drinking water will be in short supply.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0569", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "As the rain forests are de forested, the atmosphere will increase with carbon.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0577", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, woodpe cker. Woodpe ckers are birds that live in trees because they peck at the bark to find insects for food. S quirrels also live in trees, but since it' s not an option here, we go with woodpe cker as the best choice among the given options.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0585", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Wind can cause A, leaves to remain on branches. This is true because light wind s often just sh uffle the leaves without blowing them off. B, trees to stand perfectly still? That' s not right. Wind causes tree s to sway or bend, especially in stronger gusts. C, dunes at the beach to be depleted— actually, this is false too. Wind usually moves sand and builds up dunes rather than depleting them. D, still waters on the ocean? No, wind create s waves, so water is rarely still. So the correct answer is A.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 33, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0593", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The answer is C, drum.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 2, "carrier_ended": null}
