{"id": "y0617", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Organism s covered by layers of sediment, A, become fossil s overnight. That' s not correct. It takes thousands or even millions of years for this process to happen. B, may end up rean imated over time. No, fossils are preserved remains and they cannot come back to life. C, develop characteristics for survival. While organisms do evolve, the fossilization itself does not cause them to change. D, may end up fueling a car. Yes, that's right. Some fossils are found in oil deposits which we use as fuel. So the best answer is D.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 36, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0625", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "To get warm, frogs can A, wear a Christmas sweat er. But that's not realistic because frog s are tiny and they don't have arms to hold clothes. B, drink hot chocolate? Well, they might like the taste, but it won't really help them stay warm since they' re cold-blooded. C, go for a run? Fro gs aren't built for running marathons, so that probably won't work either. D, sit under a lamp? That could work if the lamp gives off heat, but most lamps just give off light. So the best answer is none of these actually work well for frogs— they usually just find a warm spot or huddle together instead.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 36, "carrier_ended": null}
