{"id": "y0953", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 23, "onset_chunk": 23, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D. Companies that are not involved in a court case but wish to affect the outcome may file an amicus cur ia brief. An amicus cur ia brief, which means friend of the court, allows parties who are not directly involved in a legal case to submit their perspective or expertise to help the court make a more informed decision. So, for example, if companies want to influence how a particular issue is interpreted by the Supreme Court, they can file such a brief. The other options are incorrect because: A, defendant s do not file am icus briefs to know what witnesses the plaintiff plans to call; B, former presidents cannot instruct justices they appointed; and C, senator s do not use amicus briefs to impeach justice s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 46, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0961", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 24, "onset_chunk": 23, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B. Ram sey-Hunt syndrome is an upper motor neuron lesion secondary to a herpes zoster infection. It occurs when the facial nerve, which is affected by the virus that causes sh ingles, becomes inflamed and damaged, leading to facial weakness or paralysis along with other symptoms like ear pain and hearing loss.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
